          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            While
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            formalizes
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence"} coherent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structures"} structures
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebra
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            %em infinite
            hierarchy of
            = succeed "-conditions," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence"} coherence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom"} axiomatized
            directly, but one needs some scheme that generates them. This turned out to be subtle.
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Finster"} Eric Finster
            had previously considered another variant of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opetopic+type+theory"} opetopic type theory
            which natively talks about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-categories"} infinity-categories
            and their higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherences"} coherences
            by type-theoretically formalizing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opetopic+sets"} opetopic sets
            %a{:href => "#Finster2018"} Finster 18
            he gives something like an implementation of aspects of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opetopic+type+theory"} opetopic type theory
            %em within
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            and provides evidence that this yields a tool to solve the general problem of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherences"} coherences
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            within
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %p
            Polynomials serve as a notion of “
            %em> higher signature
            ”. Following ideas from the categorical approach to universal algebra, we are going to encode the relations or axioms of our structure using a monadic multiplication on P.
          %h2#erics_talk Eric’s talk
          %p
            In Eric’s Agda formalisation and talk, a polynomial has its parameter sorts encoded with the parameter. We will follow a suggestion by Mike to have a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} SortOf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \SortOf
            function instead. This should make some definitions less cluttered.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I : \mathcal{U}
            be a type of sorts. A polynomial over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            consists of the following data:
          %ul
            %li
              A family of operations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                    %mo :
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Op : I \to \mathcal{U}
            %li
              For each operation, a family of parameters
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                      %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Param_i : (f : \Op i) \to \mathcal{U}
            %li
              A function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} SortOf
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                    %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \SortOf : (f : \Op i) \to \Param f \to I
          %p
            We define the type of operations of a polynomial
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            as:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Ops
                  %mo ≡
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi I
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                    %mi P
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Ops \equiv \sum_{i : I} \Op_P i
          %p
            A polynomial
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Poly
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P : \Poly I
            generates a type of trees:
          %p
            The inductive famiy
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                    %mi P
                  %mo :
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Tr_P : I \to \mathcal{U}
            has constructors
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} lf
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                      %mi P
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lf : (i : I) \to \Tr_P i
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} nd
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                      %mi P
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                      %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} SortOf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                      %mi P
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nd : (i : I) \to (f : \Op_P i) \to (\phi : (p : \Param f) \to \Tr_P (\SortOf(f,p))) \to \Tr_P i
          %p
            For a tree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                    %mi P
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w : \Tr_P i
            we define its type of leaves by induction on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Leaf
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Tr
                    %mi P
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Leaf_i : (w : Tr_P i) \to I \to \mathcal{U}
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Leaf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} lf
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≡
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi I
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Leaf( (\lf i), j) \equiv (i =_I j)
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Leaf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} nd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≡
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                        %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Leaf
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Leaf( \nd (f, \phi), j) \equiv \sum_{p : \Param f} \Leaf(\phi(p), j)
          %p and its type of nodes:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Node
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                    %mi P
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Ops
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Node_i : (w : \Tr_P i) \to \Ops \to \mathcal{U}
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Nodes
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} lf
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi jg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≡
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Nodes(\lf i, jg) \equiv \mathbf{0}
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Nodes
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} nd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi jg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≡
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi jg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                        %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Node
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi jg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Nodes(\nd(f,\phi), jg) \equiv ((i,f) = jg) + \sum_{p : \Param f} \Node(\phi(p), jg)
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                    %mi i
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w : \Tr_i P
            be a tree and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Op
                    %mi P
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Op_P i
            an operation. A frame from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is an equivalence:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Frame
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo :
                      %mi I
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Leaf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo ,
                  %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Frame(w,f) \equiv \sum_{j:I} \Leaf(w,j) \simeq \Param_i(f)
          %p i.e. the type of leaves of the tree is equivalent to the type of parameters of the operator.
          %p
            A polynomial relation for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+family"} type family
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi I
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi α
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Frame
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒰
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R :{i : I} \to (f : \Op i) \to (w : \Tr i) (\alpha : \Frame(w,f)) \to \mathcal{U}
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Poly
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P : \Poly I
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            be a relation on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P // R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Ops
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Ops
            defined as follows:
          %p
            TODO: Continue writing this out. Essentially following
            %a{:href => "https://github.com/Alizter/HoTT/blob/higher-alg/contrib/higher-alg/Polynomial3.v"} this coq file
          %h2#definitions_and_examples Definitions and Examples
          %p Here we collect the definitions and ideas that were given in Eric’s talk. We can also use the Agda formalisation for reference too.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Fix a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              of sorts. A
              %strong polynomial
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Poly
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Poly I
            %ul
              %li
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+family"} family
                of operations
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                      %mo :
                      %mi I
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒰
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Op : I \to \mathcal{U}
              %li
                For each operation, for each
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : I
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                          %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                        %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi I
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝒰
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Param_i : (f : \Op i) \to  I \to \mathcal{U}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  For
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo :
                          %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : I
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: \Op i
                  represents an operation whose output sort is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              %li
                %p
                  For
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : \Op i
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo :
                          %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : I
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : \Param_i(f, j)
                  represents an input parameter of sort
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Op i
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Param_i (f, j)
                  are not truncated at set level. So operations and parameters can have higher homotopy.
              %li
                %p
                  In
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book"} HoTT book
                  notation, we can write the previous definition as:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Poly
                    %mi I
                    %mo ≡
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                        %mo :
                        %mi I
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝒰
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Poly I \equiv \sum_{\Op : I \to \mathcal{U}}\prod_{i : I} \Param_i
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                      %mi i
                    %mo ≡
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                        %mi i
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Param_i \equiv \prod_{f : \Op i}I \to \mathcal{U}
          .num_remark
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              We start with the simplest non-trivial example, when
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ≡
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \equiv \mathbf{1}
              the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+type"} unit type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Poly
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Poly \mathbf{1}
              we clearly have
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                      %mo :
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒰
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi 𝒰
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Op : \mathbf{1} \to \mathcal{U}\simeq \mathcal{U}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Op
              is simply a type. Next we have
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Param : (f : \Op) \to \mathbf{1} \to \mathcal{U}\simeq \Op \to \mathcal{U}
              so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Param
              is just a family of types indexed over the type
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Op
            %p
              Now if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                    %mo ≡
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Fin
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Op \equiv \Fin_3
              then there would be 3 operations. Take one of these operations and call it
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi o
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o_1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Param
              would then have to chose what the type of parameters should be, let’s choose
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Fin
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Fin_2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi o
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o_1
              would be an operation (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi o
                      %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o_1 : \Op
              ) with two parameters
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Fin
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ≡
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                      %msub
                        %mi o
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : \Fin_2 \equiv \Param o_1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi o
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o_1
              is very much like the operator in an abstract syntax tree in this case.
            %p
              When the type of sorts
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              gets more structure, the objects we discuss get complicated quickly. Even letting
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                    %msub
                      %mi o
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Param o_1
              be some arbitrary type gives us an interesting object.
          %p
            A polynomial
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Poly
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P : \Poly I
            generates an associated type of trees.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The type of
              %strong trees
              associated to a polynomial
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Poly
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P : \Poly I
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+family"} inductive family
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                    %mi P
                    %mo :
                    %mi I
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Tr P : I \to \mathcal{U}
              that has constructors
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} lf
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo ,
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lf : (i : I) \to \Tr(P, i)
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} nd
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo ,
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo :
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo ,
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nd : (i : I) \to (f : \Op(P,i)) \to (\phi : (j : I) \to (p : \Param_i (f, j)) \to \Tr(P, j)) \to \Tr(P, i)
          %p
            For a tree
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w : \Tr (P, i)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The type of
              %strong leaves
              of a tree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Poly
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P : \Poly I
              is given by:
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Leaf
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi w
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi I
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒰
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Leaf : (i : I) \to (w : \Tr i) \to I \to \mathcal{U}
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Leaf
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} lf
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Leaf_i((\lf i), j) \equiv (i = j)
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "true"}
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Leaf
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} nd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≡
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo :
                            %mi I
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo :
                            %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo ,
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Leaf
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi k
                        %mo ,
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \displaystyle\Leaf_i ( \nd(f, \phi),j) \equiv \sum_{k : I} \sum_{p : \Param (f, k)} \Leaf_i ((\phi (k, p)), j)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              The type of
              %strong nodes
              of a tree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Poly
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P : \Poly I
              is given by:
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Node
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi w
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi j
                      %mo :
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                      %mi j
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Type
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Node : (i : I) \to (w : \Tr i) \to (j : I) \to \Op j \to \Type
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Node
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} lf
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Node_i ((\lf i), j, g) \equiv \mathbf{0}
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "true"}
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Node
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} nd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≡
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi j
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo :
                            %mi I
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo :
                            %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo ,
                            %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Node
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi j
                        %mo ,
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo ,
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \displaystyle \Node_i (\nd(f,\phi),j,g) \equiv ((i,f)=(j,g)) + \sum_{k : I} \sum_{p : \Param(f,k)} \Node_i ( \phi( j, p), j, g)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Poly
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P : \Poly I
              be a polynomial
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w : \Tr(P,i)
              a tree and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : \Op(P,i)
              an operation. A
              %strong frame
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family"} family
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences"} equivalences
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Frame
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Leaf
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Param
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Frame(w,f):(j:I) \to \Leaf_i(w,j) \simeq \Param(P,f,j)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em polynomial relation
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+family"} type family
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Op
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Tr
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Frame
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒰
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R : (i:I) (f:\Op i)(w : \Tr i)(\alpha : \Frame(w,f) \to \mathcal{U}
          %h2#Link References
          %ul
            %li#Finster2018
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Finster"}> Eric Finster
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Towards Higher Universal Algebra in Type Theory
                %a{:href => "https://www.uwo.ca/math/faculty/kapulkin/seminars/hottest.html"} Homotopy Type Theory Electronic Seminar
                2018 (
                %a{:href => "/nlab/files/Finster-2018-HoTTEST-compact.pdf"}> compact pdf slides
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.uwo.ca/math/faculty/kapulkin/seminars/hottestfiles/Finster-2018-12-6-HoTTEST.pdf"} original pdf slides
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hlCVHVtAlqQ"} recording
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
                code at:
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/ericfinster/higher-alg"} github.com/ericfinster/higher-alg
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://ericfinster.github.io/files/huadtt.pdf"}> Notes on a definition of higher structure
                \.
          %p
            The idea of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opetopic+sets"} opetopic sets
            that
            %a{:href => "#Finster2018"} Finster 18
            is inspired by goes back to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Dolan"} James Dolan
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higher-Dimensional Algebra III: n-Categories and the Algebra of Opetopes
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9702014"} arXiv:q-alg/9702014
